-**Outputs:** Final 2D image with intensity $I_\lambda(\hat{\mathbf{x}})$.
+**Inputs:** Volume data represented as a set of particles (voxels), each with position $\mathbf{p}_k$, density/extinction coefficient $g_k$, color $c_{\lambda k}$, and a 3D elliptical Gaussian reconstruction kernel defined by variance matrix $\mathbf{V}_k$ in object space [S6, unofficial][S11]. Camera parameters: viewing transformation matrix $\mathbf{W}$ (rotational part mapping object to camera space) and projection matrix [S6, unofficial][S11].
